summary:
For the NASA Space Apps challenge "Abandoned, but Not Forgotten," we built The Last Signal, an interactive 3D exploration experience for students aged 10–14, in English and Portuguese.

In 2047, an experimental jump strands the training ship LUMA 29 billion kilometers from Earth. With Bip, a robot companion who hides a secret, players travel home through eight destinations. Along the way they meet 20 real NASA machines left in space, such as Pioneer 10, Opportunity, Ingenuity and the Apollo landers. All images and 3D models come from NASA.

Each machine has a mission that recreates how it really worked, followed by a short diary of its history. Examples:

Pathfinder's landing sequence
Opportunity's daily energy planning
Apollo 12's science station setup
We added:

a documentary-style interface and an original design for Bip;
a pre-game checklist;
usable backpack items;
WebXR virtual reality mode;
a new recorded voice for Bip in Portuguese.
To present the project, we produced a 30-second pitch, 7-slide decks in both languages, and a full voice script.
